/// Contains an asset metric property. With metrics, you can calculate
/// aggregate functions, such as an average, maximum, or minimum, as
/// specified through an expression. A metric maps several values to a
/// single value (such as a sum). The maximum number of dependent/cascading
/// variables used in any one metric calculation is 10. Therefore, a root
/// metric can have up to 10 cascading metrics in its computational
/// dependency tree. Additionally, a metric can only have a data type of
/// DOUBLE and consume properties with data types of INTEGER or DOUBLE . For
/// more information, see Metrics in the IoT SiteWise User Guide .
